{"candidates":[{"checker_specs":[],"claim":"A decentralized network of small services is more resilient to correlated design flaws because its operators independently generate heterogeneous solutions, even if they converge on identical external dependencies.","counterconditions":["All decentralized operators independently converge on an identical internal design specification, creating a design monoculture.","The variance in internal designs is causally irrelevant because all failures are triggered by the shared external dependency.","Heterogeneous internal designs contain common, isolated security vulnerabilities due to the use of a shared code library."],"evidence_refs":[],"mechanism":"The independent operators in a decentralized network face different local constraints, team histories, and incentive gradients, leading them to generate heterogeneous internal designs. Even if they rationally converge on the same external dependencies, their distinct internal implementations act as distinct design genera. This makes them robust to correlated failures of internal design logic, unlike a monolithic service with a single design specification. Evidence would distinguish this by revealing a high variance in internal implementations among decentralized nodes while failing to find shared internal design flaws during failures.","optional_refs":["ba687c5f145e404c53a84549cf366e0b6e0106eec67404c07231357fed09e672","8929789f0ae19d5b1c2537f758719daf17f9908ce1fb0ca3fa0cc60fe9f2a2a3"],"sidecar":{"requested_context_aliases":["b541b893af0360d00b8413afc003de605643ec970a3798265e7852b357fe0cd5","286e3232567e30e109fd5626102f029c2b31c89655104a1286510b12824e4103"],"search_signal":"productive"},"typicality":0.78}],"simulation_proposals":[]}